<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs remain at 169 in the week.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs remain at 169 in the week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 169 rigs under contract in</p>
<p>the U.S. Gulf as of August 15, the same number in period ending August 8, Offshore Data Services said.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 176, was 96.0 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area was 107 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 110, a utilization rate unchanged at 97.3 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count was unchanged at 578 out of a total fleet of 605, with a utilization rate of 95.5 percent.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
